        "procedure": "A mixture of Dy2(piv)6(Hpiv)6 (700 mg, 0.45 mmol), chromium acetylacetonate (349 mg, 1 mmol), N-methyldiethanolamine (357 mg, 3 mmol), and NH4F (74 mg, 2 mmol) was stirred in 7 mL acetonitrile and 1 mL DMF in air for 15 min. The slurry was transferred into a 15-mL Teflon-lined autoclave and heated at 150 °C for 72 h, then cooled to room temperature and filtered. Red-violet block-like crystals were isolated by evaporation.",
