      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "DyC is a ferrimagnetic 3d-4f SMM. A central μ3-fluoride produces ferromagnetic Dy–Dy coupling and a ground moment of 10.7 μB, almost completely suppressing zero-field QTM. Hysteresis is observed below 5 K, with TB(ZFC) = 1.6 K, a coercive field of 1.3 T at 0.03 K (0.5 mT/s), and remanence squareness above 0.97 up to 0.7 K. Double-Orbach/Raman/QTM fitting gives U1 = 17(3) K and U2 = 38(4) K.",
